body:
Second critical-path gap in daemon/vcodecd.c handle_enc_frame(), same file as the fds:

After
  int r = n2ap_venc_encode(g.s.enc, req->in_handle, req->out_handle, N2AP_ENC_FRAME, &res);
the code immediately rejects res.bytes == 0 (line ~836, "encoder returned 0 bytes ... bad encode size"). On the real GCE daemon the ENCODE is answered with VCU_IPIMSG_ENC_ENCODE_ACK and the size/key arrive later in VCU_IPIMSG_ENC_PUT_BUFFER / venc_vsi.list_free (opus-venc and IV measured this on the plain tree); n2ap_venc_encode() therefore returns 0 bytes and the daemon fails every real frame. IV's runner already handles this and produces the validated stream.

Minimal fix (one call, includes the wait in the slow-encode measurement):

  int r = n2ap_venc_encode(g.s.enc, req->in_handle, req->out_handle, N2AP_ENC_FRAME, &res);
  if (r == 0 && n2ap_venc_wait_done != NULL && res.bytes == 0)
      r = n2ap_venc_wait_done(g.s.enc, g.hw_timeout_ms, &res);
  uint64_t elapsed = now_us() - t0;

n2ap_venc_wait_done(e, timeout_ms, &res) is in the current ap/n2ap_venc.h: it polls the PUT_BUFFER captures (cookie match, then newest-nonzero for the vendor's different cookie), returns -ETIMEDOUT on a slow job, and syncs the bitstream from device. IV uses 3000 ms; g.hw_timeout_ms (2 s) is fine if you prefer the session bound. Declare it weak only if you must link an older V41; the current tree has it strongly.

With these two fixes (fds + wait_done) the daemon path matches what the host runner already validates: 320x240 H.264, 115841 bytes, SPS/geometry/PSNR PASS.
